+
+### E15. 🟠 Handover claims cookie: the reader's groups for global-components' legacy clients (RPLT-246)
+
+**Why.** global-components' legacy CMS clients (Classic, Modern, DCF) run in IE mode and gate
+features on Entra group membership. Their only route to the reader's identity is the presence
+`whoami` (global-components' watchdog module), and the presence token is issued for the watchdog's
+app reg, so its groups (if any) are assigned to THEIR app, not ours. Our app reg is the one place
+groups are set up as feature switches (the web components read the same app-assigned groups via
+MSAL), and its id_token exists only in this callback (the refresh token never leaves it).
+
+**What.** In the IFRAME callback only, as soon as the code exchange succeeds (before the
+refresh-token check, so a failed swap or deposit doesn't cost the groups), `_claimsCookie` sets:
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Name | `cps-handover-claims` |
+| Value | `_packState({ k: "claims", v: 1, oid, iat, g: [group ids] })` — HMAC with `ENTRA_STATE_HMAC_SECRET` |
+| Groups | the id_token's `groups` claim: app-assigned only (`groupMembershipClaims: ApplicationGroup`) |
+| Path | `/global-components/presence-jsonp/whoami` only (whoami's own sub-path: never the 3 s polls) |
+| Attributes | `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax` |
+| Max-Age | the id_token's remaining life (`exp`), else 3600: the groups are as fresh as that token |
+
+- **No groups claim** (in no assigned group) or an **overage** pointer (`_claim_names`) → `g: []`,
+  logged (`drop2 entra claims — no groups claim [(overage)]`). Empty means "in none": every
+  consumer reads it as off.
+- **Over 1 KB** → not set, logged with the byte count (a handful of GUIDs is ~200 bytes).
+- **No `oid`** in the id_token → not set (nothing to bind it to).
+- Never logs a group id.
+
+**The contract (global-components' side).** whoami at `/global-components/presence-jsonp/whoami`
+verifies the HMAC with the same secret, requires `k === "claims"` and `v === 1`, and binds `oid` to
+the presence token's; anything else answers no groups (`groupsFrom` says why). The `k` marker stops
+the state and hint cookies (same secret) standing in for it. Rename or reshape only in step with
+global-components.
+
+**Prerequisite.** The `groups` optional claim on the id_token, with `ApplicationGroup` membership
+claims, on our app reg (`8d6133af` and `295ecc3c` both verified 2026-11-13). Without it every
+reader gets `g: []` — safe, just nothing switched on.
